AU  - Liepa, GU
TI  - Coronary heart disease:: How do the benefits of ω-3 fatty acids compare with those of aspirin, alcohol/red wine, and statin drugs?
T2  - JOURNAL OF THE AMERICAN OIL CHEMISTS SOCIETY
AB  - At the present time the primary cause of death of most Americans is cardiovascular disease. Approximately 20 million Americans are currently being treated with some form of statin drugs as a means to lower their blood cholesterol levels, and many of these same people also consume some combination of omega-3 FA, aspirin, and alcohol/red wine because of clinical data indicating that each of these, taken alone, seems to improve mortality. Recent studies with omega-3 FA have demonstrated a positive impact on mortality from coronary heart disease as well as from "all causes," and this article compares their metabolic benefits with those of aspirin, alcohol/red wine, and statin drugs. The article suggests that these four compounds may have synergistic qualities and that clinical trials to study this possibility are warranted.
