TI  - Omega-3 consumption may benefit heart rhythm: a review
T2  - AGRO FOOD INDUSTRY HI-TECH
AB  - Diet has been seen to have a significant impact on the development and progression of cardiovascular diseases. Fish is one of the main components of a healthy diet, while omega-3 fatty acids constitute an essential component of this fish. Experimental and clinical studies indicate that omega-3 fatty acids could act beneficially towards reduction in malignant ventricular arrhythmias, which can lead to sudden cardiac death, increase in heart rate variability, decrease risk for thrombosis, which can lead to heart attack and stroke and other effects on the hemostatic system, decrease triglyceride and remnant lipoprotein levels, improved endothelial function, as well a inhibitory effect on atherosclerosis and inflammation. As a conclusion, fish intake seems to be an important, non-pharmacologic mean, for the reduction of CVD burden.
