T2  - PROSTAGLANDINS LEUKOTRIENES AND ESSENTIAL FATTY ACIDS
CP  - 7th Fatty Acid and Cell Signaling Workshop
AB  - In this paper, we will briefly deal with the background for the possible effects of long-chain marine n-3 (also called omega-3) polyunsaturated fatty acids (PUFA) in coronary heart disease (CHD) and then focus on findings from clinical trials in humans. We will not deal with effects of alpha-linolenic acid, the non-marine type of n-3 PUFA derived from plant oils. (c) 2006 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
