TI  - Signaling through Free Fatty Acid Receptor 4 Attenuates Cardiometabolic Disease
T2  - PHYSIOLOGY
AB  - A surge in the prevalence of obesity and metabolic syndrome, which promote systemic inflammation, underlies an increase in cardiometabolic disease. Free fatty acid receptor 4 is a nutrient sensor for long-chain fatty acids, like omega 3-poly-unsaturated fatty acids (omega 3-PUFAs), that attenuates metabolic disease and resolves inflammation. Clinical trials indicate omega 3-PUFAs are cardioprotective, and this review discusses the mechanistic links between omega 3-PUFAs, free fatty acid receptor 4, and attenuation of cardiometabolic disease.
